{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"c1fb6ba6e10cf32408b2b10111707435607464f831f5e00e125267521e61a833","digest":{"component_or_area":"event_append_index_lock test","key_entities":["tests/interfaces/store/test_event_append_index_lock.py::test_contended_index_lock_cleared_during_backoff_succeeds","src/rebar/_store/event_append.py","gitutil._with_index_lock_retry","gitutil._retry_probe","_reclaim_if_stale_index_lock","threading.Timer","index.lock","_git_add","_git_commit","stage_and_commit","_is_git_lock_error"],"problem_keywords":["flaky test","test timing","race condition","index lock","macOS","py3.13"],"propositions":["Test uses wall-clock threading.Timer to release planted index.lock, which can fire after git creates its own real index.lock during commit, causing timer to unlink git's lock mid-operation and fail with 'unable to write new index file'","Failure occurs on slower runners (macOS py3.13 takes 23m24s vs ~12m Linux legs) where git commit holds lock past the 0.4s timer window","Production code with force_reclaim=True correctly reclaims the planted lock on first retry and succeeds; the failure is test-local, not a backoff or store defect","Test should use gitutil._retry_probe (deterministic probe-based lock release) instead of threading.Timer to release planted lock only after confirmed retry attempt, eliminating wall-clock timing dependency"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787397908096303001,"uuid":"36f9f459-d9ed-4f8a-a845-ad195c742301"}